module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_one_home_sweep_moves_every_row_of_that_home

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_one_home_sweep_moves_every_row_of_that_home: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_one_home_sweep_moves_every_row_of_that_home" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a wave moves ONE ambient name, but v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep scopes a run by HOME (OneHome), on the premise stated beside RosterHomeScope that one home is one name. std.algebra is the home of five rows (map_get renamed to map_lookup, and concat, count, map, join as collection_*_shape). A one-name wave's apply therefore writes imports, and refusals, for the other four names too: a wave PR silently becomes a five-name cutover whose binding diff no longer admits as ambient-to-intended-home for one name.",
    "SPECIMEN (map_get census, sleek-owl-397 on srv1, ref 6ba5eabb4b, 2026-10-23, roster_rename_census_exit home=std.algebra call=map_get): gunbc.emit_summary_map_consumer_partition reports heads=0 for map_get yet receives EDIT import std.algebra { collection_count_shape }. The edit IS site-keyed -- that file has free pipe targets `|> count` -- so the import plan is not the defect; the run's row set is. The import edits across the census carry collection_concat_shape / collection_count_shape / collection_map_shape / collection_join_shape beside map_lookup.",
    "SECOND SPECIMEN, REFUSALS FROM THE WRONG ROW: the same run refuses home-name-locally-bound in extdeps.languages.yaml.ingest (binds `count` as a parameter, yaml_key_sequence_is_clean), gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_program_view (binds `map`, program_map_member) and extdeps.cpu.ampere_altra_package (binds `map`, contact_count and siblings). None binds map_get or map_lookup; each has free map_get calls. So three files the map_get wave could edit cleanly refuse because of another row's name.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the edit is site-keyed and the guard reads a real binder; only the selected row set is wider than the wave. A heads=0 file receiving an import for the wave's home is the tell.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- found by reading the census rows before apply. HARM if missed: every wave sharing a home with another row lands that row's cutover unreviewed, and files refuse for names outside the wave.",
    "REPAIRED (still-fox-649, stacked on #14870): RosterHomeScope.OneHome carries a RosterRowSelection (EveryRowOfHome | OnlyCall { call }), so a run selects ROWS and a mutating run still names one home by construction; entries roster_import_sweep_row_exit and roster_import_sweep_apply_row_exit take the call. Controls: v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_control_row_scope, over std.algebra rows on main (map_get's rows live on the rename branch): wider-row-set (free count beside free concat; OnlyCall count imports collection_count_shape and not collection_concat_shape, the whole-home run imports both) and wrong-row-refusal (count bound as a parameter and called freely, beside a free concat; OnlyCall concat imports concat and not count, the whole-home run imports count too; it first refused home-name-locally-bound, until that guard was deleted and the offset join left the parameter alone). Each pair's whole-home half reproduces the defect, so the pair discriminates.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: a run's scope selects ROWS (home plus call), so an apply touches only the wave's row; proved by a control whose fixture has a free `|> count` and a free map_get call and must receive only the map_get edit, plus the yaml.ingest shape (a `count` parameter) coming back Clean under a map_get-only run."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "RosterHomeScope", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_control_row_scope", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_import_sweep_apply_home_exit", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_name_locally_bound", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
